WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.820
“The first rule of Bright Club is, do not
talk about Bright club.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.680
The second rule of Bright Club is: do not
talk about Bright Club.”

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.070
Excuse me for breaking that all-importing
first and second rule, but some stories are

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:19.290
just too good, too weird and wild and borderline
unbelievable, to pass up telling.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:24.060
It had been an exceptionally boring day at
the SCP Foundation, the sort of boredom not

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.910
even his usual pranks had been able to break
up, so Dr. Bright was unwinding with a good

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.880
old-fashioned movie night.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.050
He settled into his favorite overstuffed bean
bag chair, sat down a big bowl of popcorn,

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.100
and pressed play on his first flick of the
night.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.269
This one was a recommendation from Dr. Clef,
a 90s film called "Fight Club."

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:47.649
He didn't pay too much attention to the bit
about the nihilistic struggles of the modern

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:52.569
American, but when the fighting scenes started...he
couldn't help but get pumped up.

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:53.949
Look at all that punching!

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:58.069
The sight of those guys standing in a circle,
cheering each other on as they fist fought

00:00:58.069 --> 00:00:59.370
in a dark basement.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.709
It looked...awesome!

00:01:00.709 --> 00:01:05.320
Dr. Bright had seen more than enough, why
would he need to watch the last hour of the

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.320
movie?

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.880
He turned off the tv, and began outlining
a plan of his own.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.950
When he needed it the most, "Fight Club" had
given him the inspiration he so desperately

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:14.950
wanted.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:20.840
It was all so clear: He, Dr. Jack Bright,
would start his own Fight Club- but with an

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.219
SCP Foundation twist!

00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:26.950
But before he could set his plan into motion,
he needed to run it by the most logical person

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.270
he could think of.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.530
"Dr. Gears!"

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.490
He called, knocking on the man's office door.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.539
"I'm busy, Jack.

00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:33.579
What is it?"

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:36.310
Dr. Gears looked up from the stack of paperwork
in front of him.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.840
"I've been thinking...what if I started a
Fight Club of my own, here at the Foundation?"

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.080
Dr. Gears sighed heavily.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.149
"That's the worst idea I've heard all week.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:48.289
And yesterday you asked if we could leash
train SCP-682."

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:49.359
"You sure?

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:52.399
I thought it would be a really cool idea."

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:53.560
Dr. Bright pouted.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.560
"No.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.560
It's terrible.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.560
Don't do it.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.560
Could you shut the door when you leave?"

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.869
Dr. Gears took a large sip of black coffee,
and turned back to his paperwork without another

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:03.869
word.

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:07.799
Dr. Bright was a little disappointed that
Dr. Gears wasn't on board with his amazing

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:13.380
plan, but hey, in this world some people are
true visionaries, and others just can't wrap

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.600
their minds around innovative new ideas.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.960
It would have been nice to have a numbers
guy to help with the basic ins and outs of

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.860
running a Fight Club, but, like all his best
ideas, it seemed that he would just have to

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.640
handle everything himself.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.390
Gears would thank him later, when he saw firsthand
how completely awesome it was to pack a room

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.750
full of anomalies and make them fight each
other.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.760
So, now that he was resigned to his role as
a maverick, setting out on his grand venture

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.400
alone, it was time to recruit the best anomalies
he could find and assemble the ultimate Dream

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.400
Team.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.450
First, he would need a referee, someone to
keep the competitors in line and make sure

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.440
they didn't break any of his rules.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.430
Of course, he'd also have to come up with
more than two rules first, but he'd cross

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.540
that bridge when he got to it.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.680
That was Future Jack's problem.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.930
For now, who would be impartial enough, fair
and balanced enough, to keep everyone on their

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.930
best behavior?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:14.220
A proverbial lightbulb went off over Dr. Bright's
head, and he knew just who to ask.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:19.510
SCP-343, also known as God, was sitting in
the canteen and enjoying a grilled cheese

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.700
sandwich when he turned to see Dr. Bright
looking at him with the kind of beaming grin

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.070
that said "I need a favor."

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.330
"Oh, hello Jack!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.850
What can I do for you?"

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:30.850
343 asked.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.810
Dr. Bright gave him the pitch, including a
few visual aids in the form of posters he

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.850
had hastily drawn depicting various SCP battles
he hoped to see take place.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:44.040
On the final poster, he had drawn a stick
figure depiction of SCP-343, wearing a striped

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.250
uniform and holding a whistle, keeping the
peace in the ring.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.160
"So, what do you think?"

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.160
Dr. Bright asked.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.850
"You're going to go through with this whether
I agree to help or not, aren't you?"

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:56.850
God sighed.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.260
Dr. Bright nodded enthusiastically.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.790
"Alright, I'll participate.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:03.850
I don't have anything else going on today."

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:08.010
With a referee officially on board, Dr. Bright
set out to find his next recruit.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:13.680
He popped in to SCP-049's containment cell,
where the Plague Doctor was working on reanimating

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.810
a cow's heart.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.620
"Good day, Dr. Bright!"

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.209
The Plague Doctor greeted him cheerfully.

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:20.180
"You look to be in good health!"

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:25.030
Dr. Bright explained the Fight Club concept
to him, and asked if he would like to join.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.450
The Plague Doctor shook his head.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.390
"I am afraid not, my friend.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:33.370
As a physician, I took an oath to do no harm,
and to participate in such a club would be

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.830
a violation of my life's mission.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:36.830
However!

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:43.160
Should you require a doctor to treat any injuries
incurred during your club activities, I would

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:46.270
be delighted to offer you my services."

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:50.120
Dr. Bright was a bit disappointed that he
wouldn't get to see the Plague Doctor bring

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.530
his deadly touch into a combat scenario, but
he understood.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:59.500
He accepted the Doctor's offer, and moved
on to the next potential member on his list.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:04.880
He found SCP-999, the Tickle Monster, resting
in its pen after a hearty meal of chocolate

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.130
pudding and candied strawberries.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.380
It cooed delightedly at the sight of him,
oozing over to nuzzle his leg and give him

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.940
a big hug.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:17.570
He immediately felt his mood lift, and it
gave him the extra boost he knew he'd need

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.840
to see this plan through to the end!

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.560
He did his best to explain the notion of a
Fight Club to the slimy little friend, but

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.460
he couldn't be sure if the slime creature
actually understood or not.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:32.750
Either way, it was excited about the attention,
and would be following Dr. Bright around for

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.200
the rest of the day.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:38.590
Worst case scenario, he supposed it could
provide a necessary morale boost to any combatants

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:39.910
that needed it.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:44.870
He didn't have great luck recruiting his first
two ideas, so Dr. Bright decided to switch

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.150
gears a bit.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:51.190
Instead of talking to anomalies with complex
relationships to violence, or even an aversion

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:55.730
to it altogether, he would reach out to a
creature that hated absolutely everything

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.080
in the world except for violence.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:05.300
SCP-682 was in its acid bath, doing what it
did every single day: seething with rage against

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.600
all living things.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.240
"Hey there you big beautiful lizard!"

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.690
Dr. Bright called as he opened the door to
the monster's cell.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.990
Before the creature could say a single word,
he launched into his pitch.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.780
"You like fighting, don't you?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.680
Well have I got an offer for you..."

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.900
When he finished, he waited for 682's response.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:25.900
"Dissgussssting..."

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.290
It hissed.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.720
"So I'll put you down as a 'maybe' then?"

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:35.380
The creature snapped its jaws at him in response,
and he took that as his cue to leave.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:40.139
It would be enough for anyone else to get
discouraged, but once Dr. Bright had an idea,

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:41.780
he stuck to it!

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.970
At least until something better came along.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:49.450
But until he thought of a more entertaining
plan, he was all in on the SCP Fight Club.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:54.700
Thankfully, his next batch of potential members
were a lot more receptive to the idea.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:07:01.639
SCP-082 gave Dr. Bright an unsettlingly enormous
smile at the invitation, exclaiming "Perfect!

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:04.460
I was once a heavyweight champion fighter,
you know.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.800
Yes, I won many trophies over the years, I
was the very best in the sport!

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:11.690
Perhaps you've heard of me, John Sullivan
the Boston Strong Boy!"

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.490
"I thought your name was Fernand?"

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.250
Dr. Bright asked.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:16.430
"That too!"

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:22.240
After ringing SCP-662, the Butler's Hand Bell,
the attached proper English butler immediately

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.610
manifested, ready to attend to any task.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.940
"Yes, sir?"

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.490
Mr. Deeds stood at attention.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:30.490
"I need you to participate in a very special
club..."

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.090
Dr. Bright began.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:35.669
It was an offer he quite literally couldn't
refuse.

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:40.090
SCP-847, the Mannequin, was extremely receptive
to the idea.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.730
At least, Dr. Bright was pretty sure she was.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.199
She mostly responded with a series of wordless
shrieks and jerky movements.

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:49.690
But she seemed plenty ready for a good brawl!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:56.161
SCP-2273 was a bit reluctant at first, insisting
that "Combat is not a game," and "You can't

00:07:56.161 --> 00:08:01.169
fathom the things I've seen on the battlefield,
the men I held in my arms as they drew their

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:02.169
last breath."

00:08:02.169 --> 00:08:06.889
But, after a bit of spirited debate, and the
promise that all the fighting would be relatively

00:08:06.889 --> 00:08:11.870
lighthearted and not at all like his time
at war, Alexei Belitrov finally agreed to

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.420
join in on the fun.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.590
"Are we speaking of a bout of fisticuffs?"

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.460
A jaunty voice rang out.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:21.320
Dr. Bright turned to look for the source of
the sound, and the voice shouted, "Wait a

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.720
moment there old boy, you're about to step
on me!"

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:28.500
He looked down and found the person the voice
belonged to: a brightly-colored sea slug sliming

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.850
his way across the floor.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:30.850
"Oh, Lord Blackwood!

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.659
Do you want to join my fight club?"

00:08:32.659 --> 00:08:33.659
Dr. Bright asked.

00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:35.269
"Indeed it would be my pleasure!

00:08:35.269 --> 00:08:39.039
I was a member of many a private gentleman's
club in my day, and I find nothing keeps the

00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:42.199
blood pumping and the body in tip top shape
like a round of boxing!

00:08:42.199 --> 00:08:46.889
I confess I've been neglecting my fitness
of late, and this would be just the shake-up

00:08:46.889 --> 00:08:48.810
that my routine demands!

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.180
Thank you for your invitation!"

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:55.860
Dr. Bright wasn't exactly sure how SCP-1867
would be able to throw a punch when he didn't

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:58.999
have arms, but he wasn't about to question
it.

00:08:58.999 --> 00:09:02.379
Never look a gift slug in the mouth, as they
say!

00:09:02.379 --> 00:09:06.620
So far he had a giant cannibal, a supersoldier
from another universe, a living mannequin,

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.830
and a very dapper sea slug.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.410
What next…

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:14.630
Before he even had a chance to check his list,
Dr. Bright heard a robotic voice coming from

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.630
down the hall.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:19.899
"It is I, Punchbot 5000, the ultimate fighting
robot!"

00:09:19.899 --> 00:09:24.209
Now that was a perfect candidate if there
ever was one.

00:09:24.209 --> 00:09:30.079
He rounded the corner and found SCP-1370 there,
lying on its back, kicking its legs uselessly

00:09:30.079 --> 00:09:32.330
as it tried to climb back onto its feet.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.300
"I've got the perfect place for you to work
out that fighting spirit, Punchbot."

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.839
He extended a hand to help the robot up, and
it slapped the hand away.

00:09:39.839 --> 00:09:41.069
"Don't help me!

00:09:41.069 --> 00:09:42.839
I can do it myself!"

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:47.000
It insisted, and continued to struggle for
several more minutes before it finally managed

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.670
to climb back to an upright position.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:54.480
So with Pesterbot on board, Dr. Bright could
really see his vision taking shape before

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.550
his eyes.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:59.999
He followed the humming sound of a giant sun
lamp to the modified humanoid containment

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:06.050
chamber that housed the hero no one was looking
for, but the hero Dr. Bright truly needed,

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:07.779
and believed he deserved.

00:10:07.779 --> 00:10:13.790
SCP-2800 sat inside, curled up in the fetal
position beneath the glow of his lamp, soaking

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:14.790
up the rays.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.850
"Excuse me, I'm looking for Cactusman?

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.870
The spiked menace?"

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.000
Dr. Bright knocked on the door.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.519
SCP-2800 sprang into action, scrambling to
his feet at the mention of his self-given

00:10:25.519 --> 00:10:26.740
heroic moniker.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.119
"Afternoon, doc!"

00:10:28.119 --> 00:10:30.639
Cactusman rushed to the door, opening it to
let Dr. Bright in.

00:10:30.639 --> 00:10:33.199
"Looking for someone to help you crack a case?

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:34.199
Take down some criminals?

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:35.199
Bust some baddies?

00:10:35.199 --> 00:10:36.199
I'm the man for the job!

00:10:36.199 --> 00:10:38.720
The cactus man, that is!

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.010
Ha ha!"

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.730
SCP-2800 kept talking, but Dr. Bright didn't
really listen to what he was saying.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.350
All he was thinking about was how amazing
it would be to see those spikes in action

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.040
in a bare-knuckled brawl.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:54.730
Luckily, Cactusman was so starved for something
to do, for any way he could feel useful, that

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.449
he jumped at the chance to join in on the
fun.

00:10:57.449 --> 00:11:01.629
Now, Dr. Bright had really enjoyed watching
the small portion of "Fight Club" that he

00:11:01.629 --> 00:11:05.600
had seen before he got bored, but there was
one thing he didn't like about the club featured

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.600
in the movie.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.610
It was all-male.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.389
That didn't seem fair to him.

00:11:09.389 --> 00:11:12.060
Why shouldn't women get to fight too?

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:16.619
He was nothing if not a feminist - Hell, thanks
to his body-swapping necklace, he’d actually

00:11:16.619 --> 00:11:18.110
been a woman many times.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:23.869
So, he decided to seek out a few more female
anomalies to recruit.

00:11:23.869 --> 00:11:26.990
